CAT = "sfadminAutomation"; SEG = "AUT"
Q = [
('When a case is created, a field on that same case should be set from its priority as fast as possible. Which flow fits?',
 'A before-save flow', ['An after-save flow', 'A screen flow', 'A scheduled flow'],
 'Before-save (fast field update) flows change the triggering record before it is saved, without an extra save, so they are the quickest.'),
('When an opportunity closes, a related onboarding record must be created. Which flow fits?',
 'An after-save flow', ['A before-save flow', 'A screen flow', 'A validation rule'],
 'After-save flows can create and update related records and run actions. Before-save flows can only update the triggering record.'),
('Agents need a step-by-step form that asks questions and creates a case at the end. Which flow type fits?',
 'A screen flow', ['A record-triggered flow', 'A scheduled flow', 'A platform event flow'],
 'Screen flows show screens to users and can be launched from Lightning pages, quick actions or the utility bar.'),
('Every night at 2 a.m., stale open leads should be marked Inactive. Which flow type fits?',
 'A schedule-triggered flow', ['A screen flow', 'A before-save flow on Lead', 'A platform event-triggered flow'],
 'Schedule-triggered flows run at a set time and frequency, optionally for each record in a filtered batch.'),
('Which flow type runs only when another flow, Apex or an API call starts it?',
 'An autolaunched flow', ['A screen flow', 'A record-triggered flow', 'A schedule-triggered flow'],
 'Autolaunched flows with no trigger run when invoked, for example as a subflow, from Apex or from the REST API.'),
('A follow-up task should be created 30 days after an opportunity closes. What should the admin add to the record-triggered flow?',
 'A scheduled path', ['A screen element', 'A loop element', 'A fault path'],
 'Scheduled paths run part of an after-save record-triggered flow at a time relative to the trigger or a date field on the record.'),
('Which entry setting must a record-triggered flow use to have a scheduled path that fires only once per qualifying change?',
 'Only when updated to meet them', ['Every time it is updated', 'Before the record is saved', 'When the record is deleted'],
 'Scheduled paths need the flow to run only when a record is created, or updated to meet its conditions, so it does not reschedule on every edit.'),
('Which flow element retrieves records from the database so later elements can use them?',
 'Get Records', ['Assignment', 'Decision', 'Screen'],
 'Get Records queries records that meet conditions and stores one record or a collection for later steps.'),
("A flow must take different paths depending on a field's value. Which element fits?",
 'Decision', ['Loop', 'Assignment', 'Get Records'],
 'Decision elements evaluate conditions and send the flow down the outcome that matches.'),
('A flow updates a collection of 300 records. What is the best practice for the update?',
 'Update once after the loop', ['Update inside the loop', 'Use one flow per record', 'Use a screen for each record'],
 'Placing Update Records inside a loop can hit governor limits. Change values in the loop, add records to a collection, and update the collection once after it.'),
('Which element sets or changes values of variables inside a flow?',
 'Assignment', ['Decision', 'Screen', 'Get Records'],
 'Assignment elements set, add to or change variables and record fields held in the flow, without saving to the database.'),
('A flow fails sometimes on an update and the admin wants it to send an alert instead of an error screen. What should be added?',
 'A fault path', ['A scheduled path', 'A second version', 'A decision outcome'],
 'Fault paths connect from data and action elements to steps that run when the element fails, such as sending an email.'),
('A record-triggered flow should run only when Stage changes to Closed Won, not on every edit. Which resource lets the flow compare old and new values?',
 '$Record__Prior', ['$User', '$Flow.CurrentDate', 'A text template'],
 "$Record__Prior holds the record's values before the change, so the flow can check whether a field actually changed."),
("An admin wants to see a flow's path step by step with test values before activating it. What should be used?",
 'Debug in Flow Builder', ['Setup Audit Trail', 'Health Check', 'Login History for users'],
 "Flow Builder's Debug runs the flow with chosen inputs, can run as another user and roll back changes, and shows each step."),
('An admin edits an active flow and saves. What happens?',
 'A new version is saved', ['The active one changes at once', 'The flow is deleted', 'All versions activate'],
 'Saving changes to a flow creates a new version; only one version is active until the admin activates the new one.'),
('Several record-triggered flows run on Opportunity and the admin needs to set their order. Where can she see and order them?',
 'Flow Trigger Explorer', ['Schema Builder', 'Report Builder', 'The Setup Audit Trail'],
 'Flow Trigger Explorer lists record-triggered flows for an object and context, and the Trigger Order value sets their run order.'),
('The org still has workflow rules and Process Builder processes. What does Salesforce recommend?',
 'Move them to Flow', ['Copy them to Apex', 'Keep adding new ones', 'Convert them to reports'],
 'Salesforce has retired workflow rules and Process Builder in favour of Flow and offers the Migrate to Flow tool to convert them.'),
('Which tool converts existing workflow rules into record-triggered flows?',
 'Migrate to Flow', ['Data Loader', 'Change sets', 'Schema Builder'],
 'Migrate to Flow, in Setup, converts workflow rules and many processes into flows that the admin then tests and activates.'),
("Discounts over 30% need a manager's sign-off, and the record must be locked while it waits. Which feature fits?",
 'An approval process', ['A validation rule on Discount', 'A sharing rule on Opportunity', 'A duplicate rule'],
 'Approval processes route a record to approvers in steps and lock it during approval, with actions on submission, approval and rejection.'),
('In an approval process, which actions run when the record is first sent for approval?',
 'Initial submission actions', ['Final approval actions', 'Recall actions', 'Final rejection actions'],
 'Initial submission actions run when a record is submitted, for example locking it and updating a status field.'),
('An approver will be on holiday for two weeks. What lets someone else approve her requests?',
 'A delegated approver', ['A frozen user', 'A muting permission set', 'A queue owner change'],
 'Each user can name a delegated approver, who can approve or reject requests on their behalf when the process allows it.'),
('Which approvers can an approval step route a request to?',
 'A manager, user or queue', ['Only the system admin', 'Only the record owner', 'Only a public group'],
 "Approval steps can route to the submitter's manager (or another user hierarchy field), specific users, queues or a related user."),
('A user should be told in the Salesforce bell and on the mobile app when a large deal closes. Which flow action fits?',
 'Send Custom Notification', ['Post to a list view', 'Update a report chart', 'Create a sandbox copy'],
 'The Send Custom Notification action sends desktop and mobile notifications using a custom notification type.'),
('Which runs first when a record is saved: a before-save record-triggered flow or custom validation rules?',
 'The before-save flow', ['The validation rules', 'They run together', 'Whichever was made first'],
 'In the order of execution, before-save flows run before custom validation rules, so validation checks the values the flow set.'),
('An external system publishes a message when a shipment leaves, and Salesforce should react. Which flow trigger fits?',
 'A platform event flow', ['A screen flow', 'A schedule-triggered flow', 'A before-save flow'],
 'Platform event-triggered flows subscribe to a platform event and run when a matching event message is received.'),
('A requirement only says that Close Date cannot be in the past when a deal is saved. What is the simplest solution?',
 'A validation rule', ['A screen flow', 'An approval process', 'A scheduled flow'],
 'Blocking bad data at save time is what validation rules are for; flow is for actions and updates.'),
('In a screen flow, which resource builds a picklist of options from records, such as active products?',
 'A collection choice set', ['A text template', 'A constant', 'A stage resource'],
 'Collection choice sets (and record choice sets) generate choices for screen components from a collection of records.'),
('A screen flow updates records the user cannot normally edit. What does this depend on?',
 "The flow's run context", ["The user's page layout", 'The report folder', 'The compact layout'],
 'Flows can run in user context or in system context with or without sharing. Screen flows run in user context unless the admin changes it.'),
('A screen flow should be one click away for agents on every page of the console. Where can the admin add it?',
 'The utility bar', ['A report folder', 'A list view filter', 'A matching rule'],
 "Flows can be added to an app's utility bar, as well as to Lightning pages and quick actions."),
('A flow should email the account owner using a saved template whenever a case is escalated. Which action fits?',
 'Send Email', ['Get Records', 'Assignment', 'A Loop'],
 'Flows can send email with the Send Email action or by calling an email alert that uses an email template.'),
]
